# GIVING AN EXTENT IN 3D, AND LETTING IT WORK OUT THE PIXELS.
#
#   python3 -m sparkblocks run t3-extent-3d.spark
#
# `box 4 3 2` is not a picture. It is an EXTENT -- 4 wide, 3 high,
# 2 deep -- handed over as points in space.
#
#   flat   drops xyz onto the grid, so 3D becomes 2D
#   plot   lights whichever pixel each point lands on
#
# You never name a pixel. You say where things ARE, and their
# location decides which pixels come on.
#
# Try: change `box 4 3 2` to `ball 2`, or the numbers to `box 8 1 1`.

screen fit
box 4 3 2
spin y 30
spin x 20
flat
plot
draw
